WEBVTT

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:03.940
No Entry

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:06.410
What's our next class again?

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:07.480
Math?

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:10.000
When is math ever gonna be useful to us?

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:10.940
Seriously.

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:13.990
I told you, don't touch my hair!

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:16.110
Hey! What are you doing?!

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:24.260
<i>When our eyes met, 
we'd always look away once...</i>

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:30.620
<i>Then we'd make eye contact again.</i>

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:35.840
<i>That was Kou and I in our 
first year of middle school.</i>

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:39.310
<i>Nobody else knew...</i>

00:00:41.830 --> 00:00:44.050
<i>...about those times we 
fumbled through together.</i>

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:22.320
<i>I want to see Kou!</i>

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:24.330
<i>I want to talk to Kou!</i>

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:29.900
<i>These are the advanced course 
students' shoe boxes...</i>

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:31.570
Who are you looking for?

00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:38.350
Kou!

00:02:41.350 --> 00:02:43.350
I was looking for you!

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:45.360
There's something I wanted you to hear.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:48.360
What, that you made up with 
your friends or something?

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:50.650
No, that didn't work out.

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:51.270
Oh?

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:56.610
But I think it's natural that not 
everything you try will go well, right?

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:59.680
So, I'm gonna start again from scratch.

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:01.860
I think that's for the best!

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:05.370
I'm glad.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:08.440
Kou!

00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:13.090
Hey, I was still talking to you.

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:15.540
Hey! You're that girl from before.

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:17.810
Oh, hey.

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:20.650
If it's about that thing from 
before, it's already done.

00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:22.020
Give it up already.

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:24.300
It's not about that.

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:29.270
As I was saying, I'll be coming by 
to cook today, so please be at home.

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:34.620
And I'll be staying the night, too.

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:35.610
Staying the night?!

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:41.100
<i>Guh! Could that mean... that they're...?</i>

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:44.700
Idiot. What are you thinking about?

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:48.770
My big brother.

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:54.960
We weren't really hiding it, 
but we also don't advertise it, I guess.

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:57.740
I guess most people don't know about it.

00:03:59.070 --> 00:04:00.150
<i>His brother!</i>

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:02.070
<i>Of course! I thought they looked alike!</i>

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:04.120
Are you two dating?

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:08.180
Huh? Dating someone who eats more than me?

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:09.310
No way.

00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:13.270
You loved me when we were 
in middle school, though!

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:16.020
<i>You</i> loved <i>me.</i>

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:18.560
You said you loved me too, though!

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:19.740
Oh, that?

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:22.150
That was a lie. I just got 
caught up in the moment.

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:26.080
Huh? But you totally made eye contact.

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:29.010
Are you sure that wasn't just because 
of how you were staring at me?

00:04:32.110 --> 00:04:33.210
This is stupid.

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:35.930
Either way, it's not relevant now.

00:04:35.930 --> 00:04:37.210
Running away!

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:41.160
At least, I can tell you're close.

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:43.380
Um, Miss...?

00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:45.530
Yoshioka Futaba.

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:49.210
That's a nice name. Futaba, huh?

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:52.310
Futaba, huh...

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:54.290
Futaba...

00:04:56.590 --> 00:04:59.070
Oh, Futaba-san!

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:02.050
A teacher's making a pass at a student.

00:05:02.050 --> 00:05:02.440
What?!

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:03.530
What?!

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:07.860
No... I wasn't!

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:15.910
No, no! I really wasn't!

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:20.440
Darn it.

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:23.760
Yoshioka Futaba, huh?

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:31.180
Yoshioka Futaba

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:38.080
Yoshioka Futaba?

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:39.860
Who's that?

00:05:42.470 --> 00:05:43.320
Don't look!

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:45.500
What? Is that a girl you like?

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:47.030
Shut up!

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:52.190
I see.

00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:58.870
So you don't live with Tanaka-sensei?

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:03.300
For now, since we're student 
and teacher at the same school.

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:06.370
Kou, you moved out on your own?

00:06:06.370 --> 00:06:08.800
No... my brother moved out.

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:11.680
Then you're back in your old house?

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:12.640
Yeah.

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:14.880
With your mom?

00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:17.270
Just me.

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:18.810
Why don't you change your family name ba—

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:22.730
I've had enough.

00:06:23.660 --> 00:06:26.440
You're so annoying. 
It's none of your business.

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:31.660
N-None of my business? 
You're the one who brought me into it!

00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:40.540
There.

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:42.190
I let you go. It's fine now, right?

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:47.880
<i>Kou. Why...</i>

00:06:49.450 --> 00:06:53.410
<i>Right now... we're making eye contact...</i>

00:06:54.130 --> 00:06:57.510
<i>But it feels like he's not 
really looking anywhere.</i>

00:07:01.040 --> 00:07:03.470
Didn't you want me to let go?

00:07:05.630 --> 00:07:08.250
So... let me go.

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:13.440
<i>Where is Kou's heart right now?</i>

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:19.870
Y-You disappeared all of a sudden, 
then reappeared all of a sudden...

00:07:20.890 --> 00:07:24.250
I have a lot of things I want to ask you!

00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:29.890
There's so much I haven't been able 
to get straight in my mind!

00:07:34.390 --> 00:07:35.310
You're so annoying.

00:07:36.830 --> 00:07:38.750
I told you not to cry.

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:42.820
Sorry.

00:07:46.420 --> 00:07:47.720
Kou?

00:07:47.720 --> 00:07:49.310
The summer festival.

00:07:51.460 --> 00:07:53.060
That day at Sankaku Park.

00:07:54.560 --> 00:07:56.600
Did you wait for me?

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:07.130
I did wait for you.

00:08:07.510 --> 00:08:10.130
I waited so long.

00:08:11.660 --> 00:08:14.440
Yeah. I'm sorry.

00:08:15.570 --> 00:08:19.680
I thought you hated boys, so...

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:20.720
That was just...

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:26.190
No. I still meant to go to 
Sankaku Park that day.

00:08:26.190 --> 00:08:32.230
But right after summer vacation began,
 we had trouble at home.

00:08:32.230 --> 00:08:33.830
Things got complicated.

00:08:40.380 --> 00:08:44.060
I'm sorry I couldn't make it that day.

00:08:49.490 --> 00:08:50.460
Kou...

00:08:51.860 --> 00:08:55.920
<i>That's right. A lot of things 
happened in Kou's life.</i>

00:08:55.920 --> 00:09:01.010
<i>A lot more than mine. And yet I...</i>

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:03.230
I'm sorry.

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:06.320
I was insensitive, and asked too much.

00:09:07.300 --> 00:09:08.340
It's okay.

00:09:11.520 --> 00:09:12.650
Wanna go home?

00:09:15.110 --> 00:09:16.040
Yeah.

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:33.420
Caution

00:09:32.780 --> 00:09:33.420
Bye.

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:35.400
I have to go this way, so...

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:36.160
Sure.

00:09:39.620 --> 00:09:40.350
Kou!

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:44.650
You're looking forward 
to dinner tonight, right?

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:45.240
Huh?

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:47.250
Don't say "huh!"

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:50.060
Because Tanaka-sensei's 
coming to cook for you, right?

00:09:50.060 --> 00:09:53.780
Oh, that's right. My brother's coming.

00:09:55.680 --> 00:09:57.900
So long! Bye bye!

00:10:01.850 --> 00:10:05.910
<i>I'm so happy! Kou talked about himself to me.</i>

00:10:17.590 --> 00:10:19.550
<b>Tanaka</b>

00:10:17.590 --> 00:10:19.550
Mabuchi

00:10:23.010 --> 00:10:26.980
<b>Tartar Sauce</b>

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:39.560
Kou age 12 
 Youichi age 11 
 Kou age 11 
 Youichi age 10 
 Kou age 10 
 Youichi age 9 
 Kou age 9 
 Youichi age 8 
 Kou age 8

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:43.770
Your big brother's waiting.

00:10:45.670 --> 00:10:46.860
Always...

00:11:08.250 --> 00:11:14.110
<i>That's right. If you lose something,
 just build it again.</i>

00:11:16.050 --> 00:11:18.460
<i>And this time, with greater care.</i>

00:11:21.470 --> 00:11:25.690
<i>Starting today, I'm going to 
rebuild everything from scratch.</i>

00:11:26.110 --> 00:11:29.510
Yoshioka... Yoshioka...

00:11:29.510 --> 00:11:31.480
There I am! Class 2.

00:11:31.740 --> 00:11:32.180
Ah!

00:11:32.230 --> 00:11:35.670
Makita Yuuri 
 Murao Shuuko 
 Yoshioka Futaba

00:11:34.060 --> 00:11:35.130
Makita-san!

00:11:36.220 --> 00:11:38.000
<i>It's starting today!</i>

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:41.630
Okay!

00:11:41.630 --> 00:11:42.620
<i>Let's get started!</i>

00:11:44.780 --> 00:11:45.850
Yoshioka-san!

00:11:50.230 --> 00:11:51.580
Oh, yeah!

00:11:51.580 --> 00:11:52.850
Murao!

00:11:52.850 --> 00:11:56.200
We're in the same class again!
 Nice to see you!

00:11:56.670 --> 00:11:57.570
Hello.

00:11:57.910 --> 00:11:59.290
During our first year,

00:11:59.290 --> 00:12:02.010
you said you didn't want to remember 
anything about your class.

00:12:02.750 --> 00:12:06.870
But I won't let you say that about your 
second-year class! No matter what!

00:12:10.910 --> 00:12:13.870
Looks like there's an 
overbearing guy in our class.

00:12:16.080 --> 00:12:17.250
Kou!

00:12:17.600 --> 00:12:18.500
Hey.

00:12:21.590 --> 00:12:23.800
After class today, you wanna—

00:12:21.900 --> 00:12:23.810
<i>What? Why?</i>

00:12:24.410 --> 00:12:29.000
<i>I'm... in the same class as Kou?!</i>

00:12:39.490 --> 00:12:40.540
Morning!

00:12:41.140 --> 00:12:43.030
So sleepy.

00:12:44.370 --> 00:12:45.960
<i>It's starting.</i>

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:49.950
<i>I won't get so fixated on 
surface-only friendships</i>

00:12:50.210 --> 00:12:52.450
<i>that I pretend to be someone I'm not.</i>

00:12:53.240 --> 00:12:56.390
<i>In my new class, I'll build 
it over from scratch!</i>

00:12:56.390 --> 00:13:00.630
Hey. How does it feel to fall from 
advanced classes into regular ones?

00:13:01.660 --> 00:13:03.280
What do you mean?

00:13:03.830 --> 00:13:07.340
Aren't you thinking "Why do I have to hang out 
with these dummies" or something?

00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:13.540
<i>Wow, that's a backhanded way 
of putting it. Crafty jerk.</i>

00:13:14.030 --> 00:13:17.640
What do you mean? 
I'm not especially smart, you know.

00:13:17.640 --> 00:13:18.100
Huh?

00:13:18.100 --> 00:13:24.070
In middle school, I really worked 
myself to death studying.

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:27.020
When I got into high school, 
I relaxed just a little.

00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:30.980
Then before I knew it, 
my grades totally dropped.

00:13:33.380 --> 00:13:35.870
Mabuchi, you're Tanaka's 
younger brother, right?

00:13:35.870 --> 00:13:36.620
Yeah.

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:38.720
I thought you looked alike.

00:13:38.720 --> 00:13:42.020
<i>Wow, he navigated that one really well.</i>

00:13:42.020 --> 00:13:44.670
<i>I guess he's really good at setting 
the atmosphere of a place.</i>

00:13:54.820 --> 00:13:55.770
What's wrong?

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:58.230
Oh, nothing.

00:13:58.830 --> 00:14:01.440
<i>What's with that? Is he in elementary school?</i>

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:07.180
<i>Just like he's in elementary school, huh...</i>

00:14:12.400 --> 00:14:13.660
Morning!

00:14:13.980 --> 00:14:14.660
Morning!

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:17.090
Hey, you see that girl?

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:21.960
I hear that in the first year, 
all the girls avoided her.

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:23.370
Huh? How come?

00:14:23.370 --> 00:14:26.260
I dunno why, but there 
must be something, right?

00:14:29.510 --> 00:14:33.970
<b>Forward</b>

00:14:29.870 --> 00:14:33.430
<i>She's... pretending it 
doesn't bother her, right?</i>

00:14:35.080 --> 00:14:37.670
<i>It's pretty easy to sway 
someone's opinion, huh?</i>

00:14:38.920 --> 00:14:41.340
<i>That includes mine, too...</i>

00:14:42.490 --> 00:14:45.970
<i>I could create an atmosphere that will keep
Makita-san from getting excluded!</i>

00:14:46.510 --> 00:14:47.860
Hey, Makita-san!

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:53.530
Look, look! The thing you gave me before.

00:14:53.840 --> 00:14:55.880
Oh, you put it on?

00:14:56.490 --> 00:14:58.100
Thank you!

00:14:56.490 --> 00:15:00.210
<b>EEEE!</b>

00:14:58.100 --> 00:15:00.210
No, thank <i>you!</i>

00:15:00.210 --> 00:15:03.110
What? She's just talking normally.

00:15:03.110 --> 00:15:04.710
She doesn't seem that bad to me.

00:15:04.710 --> 00:15:07.010
<i>Okay! That's going well!</i>

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:08.300
<i>Now, let's keep it up...</i>

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:10.510
Oh, that girl!

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:12.060
At the end of first year,

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:16.010
That Girl

00:15:12.060 --> 00:15:14.270
I hear she had a big fight 
with some girls in her class.

00:15:14.270 --> 00:15:16.010
Oh? Is she a scary person?

00:15:16.010 --> 00:15:17.980
She has pretty severe features...

00:15:17.980 --> 00:15:20.250
Is she a delinquent? Seriously?

00:15:20.250 --> 00:15:23.980
<i>I might have severe features, 
but I'm not a delinquent!</i>

00:15:23.980 --> 00:15:27.910
<i>Did I just create an atmosphere 
where I would get excluded?!</i>

00:15:33.620 --> 00:15:36.990
Murao-san! M-Morning!

00:15:37.990 --> 00:15:39.290
Morning.

00:15:41.420 --> 00:15:43.580
<i>She seems surprisingly approachable!</i>

00:15:43.580 --> 00:15:44.000
Murao-sa—

00:15:45.360 --> 00:15:45.920
The Rowdy Gang Leader Goes on a Journey

00:15:46.440 --> 00:15:49.880
"Don't Address 
Me Again" aura

00:15:49.880 --> 00:15:52.490
<i>I've been totally blocked out!</i>

00:15:52.490 --> 00:15:55.320
Murao! Morning!

00:15:55.320 --> 00:15:58.310
Whatcha readin'? Whatcha listenin' to?

00:16:01.810 --> 00:16:03.310
I was thinking,

00:16:03.310 --> 00:16:06.970
we really are lucky to be in 
the same class in our second year, too.

00:16:06.970 --> 00:16:08.520
<i>That fruitless attempt at conversation...</i>

00:16:08.520 --> 00:16:10.610
<i>It'll reflect on me, too, so please stop!</i>

00:16:10.610 --> 00:16:15.530
That's right! The other day 
I went shopping, and...

00:16:25.920 --> 00:16:28.380
I can't seem to get moving.

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:30.570
How's your new class?

00:16:31.470 --> 00:16:33.560
Oh... um...

00:16:34.150 --> 00:16:38.170
Well, how to put it... 
a lot of things aren't bearing fruit.

00:16:38.830 --> 00:16:40.880
How about volunteering for 
class representative?

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:45.850
I'm not really cut out 
for that sort of thing.

00:16:46.180 --> 00:16:49.860
Your high school life will be 
over before you know it.

00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:51.900
There are things you can only do now.

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:53.940
You should do as many of them as you can.

00:17:00.330 --> 00:17:03.760
Still... easier said than done...

00:17:01.040 --> 00:17:05.470
<b>Full-Packed Kalbi Bread</b>

00:17:03.760 --> 00:17:05.120
How gloomy!

00:17:07.460 --> 00:17:10.920
<b>Coffee</b>

00:17:07.800 --> 00:17:09.070
Kou...

00:17:09.070 --> 00:17:10.920
You depressed?

00:17:12.220 --> 00:17:15.630
I can't find a foothold to take a first step.

00:17:17.280 --> 00:17:20.230
I even got labeled a scary person.

00:17:21.700 --> 00:17:25.650
Of course, I know you're 
really a wishy-washy person.

00:17:26.160 --> 00:17:29.310
That doesn't make me look any better.

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:33.030
Oh? I wasn't trying to make you look better.

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:37.570
You talked about starting from scratch,

00:17:37.570 --> 00:17:39.520
and this is how you're acting on day one?

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:43.550
Day one made me realize how helpless I am.

00:17:46.230 --> 00:17:47.710
Well, what's the big deal?

00:17:47.710 --> 00:17:50.990
If you get crushed that quickly, 
it won't bother anyone.

00:17:55.130 --> 00:18:00.610
And by the same token, if you don't give up,
 it won't bother anyone either.

00:18:02.310 --> 00:18:05.280
After all, nothing's started yet.

00:18:06.440 --> 00:18:08.280
Just do what you want.

00:18:09.360 --> 00:18:14.700
<i>Nothing's started yet. 
I haven't started anything, either.</i>

00:18:15.980 --> 00:18:19.320
<i>If I really want to start something new...</i>

00:18:20.610 --> 00:18:22.780
<i>...it goes without saying that I'll need</i>

00:18:22.780 --> 00:18:26.500
<i>more power than usual to get things going.</i>

00:18:22.780 --> 00:18:26.500
<b>Class Representatives 

00:18:26.940 --> 00:18:29.420
No candidates at all?

00:18:34.280 --> 00:18:38.270
The longer you wait, 
the later you'll be getting home.

00:18:39.340 --> 00:18:41.900
I'm no happier about it than you are.

00:18:44.300 --> 00:18:46.100
<i>Because you can't get things going...</i>

00:18:49.970 --> 00:18:52.590
<i>...if things always stay the same!</i>

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:57.470
Oh, Yoshioka. You want to do it?

00:18:57.470 --> 00:18:58.030
Yes!

00:18:58.650 --> 00:19:01.990
Okay, Yoshioka will be our 
female class representative.

00:19:02.520 --> 00:19:04.600
Yoshioka, you take over the procedure.

00:19:05.060 --> 00:19:06.200
Sure.

00:19:08.990 --> 00:19:12.540
<i>I want to start something!</i>

00:19:16.050 --> 00:19:19.510
<b>Class Representatives:
 Yoshioka Futaba 

00:19:17.830 --> 00:19:19.510
Okay! Well!

00:19:19.510 --> 00:19:23.640
I'd like to pick a male class representative.

00:19:23.640 --> 00:19:25.470
Any candidates?

00:19:31.120 --> 00:19:34.650
Someone who will really 
fire up the class with me?

00:19:34.650 --> 00:19:35.970
Please!

00:19:36.880 --> 00:19:38.700
<i>Guess I gotta...</i>

00:19:39.580 --> 00:19:41.700
I don't mind doing it.

00:19:44.790 --> 00:19:45.500
<i>Kou!</i>

00:19:48.720 --> 00:19:51.810
If there's no one else, Mabuchi-kun it is!

00:19:55.920 --> 00:19:58.130
<i>He got the jump on me.</i>

00:19:58.500 --> 00:20:01.440
Well, Mabuchi-kun. Please join 
me in handling the procedure.

00:20:03.190 --> 00:20:04.550
Go for it, Kou.

00:20:05.550 --> 00:20:06.840
What?

00:20:06.840 --> 00:20:09.560
N-Nothing...

00:20:09.880 --> 00:20:12.050
Th-Thanks.

00:20:12.050 --> 00:20:16.260
Dummy. I just wanted you to pick 
so we could go home sooner.

00:20:17.150 --> 00:20:18.830
Let's get the rest picked already.

00:20:19.890 --> 00:20:23.580
We need three event representatives! 
Anyone wanna do it?

00:20:25.440 --> 00:20:28.050
I-I'll do it.

00:20:28.720 --> 00:20:29.520
Makita-san?

00:20:29.520 --> 00:20:32.310
You'll do it?! Thank you!

00:20:32.310 --> 00:20:33.920
That's a big help!

00:20:36.250 --> 00:20:38.690
Well? Two more.

00:20:45.580 --> 00:20:46.840
Murao-san?

00:20:47.790 --> 00:20:49.930
I'll be an event representative.

00:20:51.670 --> 00:20:55.870
<i>Murao-san... if she's in, 
then next up is...</i>

00:20:56.700 --> 00:21:00.320
Yes! I'll be an event representative, too!

00:21:00.950 --> 00:21:01.950
<i>Knew it!</i>

00:21:13.540 --> 00:21:15.750
<i>That happened really fast.</i>

00:21:15.750 --> 00:21:17.670
<i>But even so, what a strong group.</i>

00:21:18.240 --> 00:21:21.630
Okay. Class representatives 
and event representatives

00:21:21.630 --> 00:21:23.630
will need to participate 
in leadership training.

00:21:23.970 --> 00:21:25.610
Leadership training?

00:21:25.610 --> 00:21:29.760
It's an overnight workshop. 
Tanaka-sensei runs it.

00:21:36.030 --> 00:21:39.160
What? You have something to say?

00:21:39.820 --> 00:21:41.610
N-Nothing.

00:21:43.300 --> 00:21:46.970
<i>It's starting. I'm starting it!</i>

00:21:46.970 --> 00:21:48.570
<i>Something I can only do now!</i>

00:21:48.570 --> 00:21:54.970
<b>Class
 Representatives:
 Yoshioka Futaba 
 Mabuchi Kou 

00:21:49.610 --> 00:21:53.870
<i>From this moment forward... 
with these members!</i>

00:23:26.000 --> 00:23:41.020
Next Episode . . .

00:23:28.470 --> 00:23:33.340
I hope that someday, when I remember this,
 the people I shared it with

00:23:34.420 --> 00:23:38.740
will see it as a "happy memory" 
with the same warmth that I do.
